----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let a = 1000

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let c = a /! 10

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let d = a + 1

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let e = a + 2

----------
expect all four units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `a` = 1000 |
| 2 | reads `a` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 100 |
| 3 | reads `a` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `d` = 1001 |
| 4 | reads `a` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `e` = 1002 |

----------
scriptunit-edit 3
----------

let d = a

----------
expect unit 3 is edited to take `a`
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | `a` is as unit 1 made it | `a` moved |
| 2 | reads `a` (1) | untouched | reads `a` before the take | `c` = 100 |
| 3 | takes `a` (1) | recompiles, runs | edited | `d` = 1000 |
| 4 | reads `a` (1) | recompile fails | `a` was given away by unit 3 | - |

----------
scriptunit-edit 3
----------

let d = a + 1

----------
expect unit 3 is edited back to read `a`
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rewind: unit 3 took `a` when it last ran, and the edit undoes that | `a` = 1000 |
| 2 | reads `a` (1) | untouched | unit 1 built the same `a` | `c` = 100 |
| 3 | reads `a` (1) | recompiles, runs | edited | `d` = 1001 |
| 4 | reads `a` (1) | reruns | `a` can be named again, as it could in step 1, whose compile is still memoized | `e` = 1002 |
